# Documentation & Naming

## Code Comments (English only)

- Write comments in **clear, fluent English** — not telegraphic
- Explain **why** and non-obvious **how**; do not restate the code
- Comment: i18n edge cases, SEO/metadata helpers, email adapter behavior, honeypot anti-spam
- Public utilities: short JSDoc with purpose and params
- No commented-out dead code — delete it; git has history
- UI strings belong in `messages/*.json`, never in comments as user-facing copy

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
// hreflang alternates must include x-default pointing to English for international discovery.

// ❌ BAD
// set title
```

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files (TS) | kebab-case | `locale-switcher.tsx`, `email.adapter.ts` |
| React components | PascalCase file + export | `ProjectCard.tsx` |
| Functions / variables | camelCase, verb-led | `formatDate`, `getProjects` |
| Types / interfaces | PascalCase | `Project`, `BlogPostMeta` |
| Constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE or camel | `SITE_NAME`, `defaultLocale` |
| NestJS modules | `<feature>.module.ts` | `contact.module.ts` |
| i18n keys | dot.nested.camelCase | `projects.viewSite`, `hero.cta.contact` |
| Blog slugs | kebab-case | `websocket-trading-state` |

Names must be **meaningful** — prefer `experience-timeline.tsx` over `section3.tsx`.

## Project Documentation (bilingual pairs)

Every doc exists as two files:

| English | Persian |
|---------|---------|
| `DOCUMENTNAME.md` | `DOCUMENTNAME.FA.md` |

**Primary entry points:** `README.md` + `README.FA.md` at repo root.

Add focused docs when an area grows (`docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` + `docs/DEPLOYMENT.FA.md`, `docs/CONTENT.md` + `docs/CONTENT.FA.md`). Keep **content in sync** — same sections and facts; only language differs.

### Language switcher (first line of every bilingual doc)

```markdown
<p align="right"><strong>English</strong> · <a href="./README.FA.md">فارسی</a></p>
```

Persian file:

```markdown
<p align="right"><a href="./README.md">English</a> · <strong>فارسی</strong></p>
```

## When to Update Docs

Update the relevant `.md` / `.FA.md` pair in the **same change** when you:

- Add/remove pages, API routes, or env variables
- Change i18n routing, contact flow, or deploy steps
- Alter folder structure
- Lock a new architectural decision

Skip doc updates for trivial typo fixes unless they affect setup instructions.

## Doc Quality

- Complete enough for a new developer (or future you) to run the project
- Include: purpose, prerequisites, commands, env vars, links to Cursor rules
- Root README: stack, structure, dev commands, link to `AGENTS.md`

## Agent / Contributor Checklist

Before finishing a significant task:

1. Code comments where logic is non-obvious
2. Names reviewed for clarity
3. Matching EN + FA doc files updated if user-facing setup changed
4. `content-branding.mdc` facts respected — no invented copy
5. i18n keys added for both `en.json` and `fa.json` when adding UI strings
